        <div id="capacity" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. Bushel Capacity: What 6, 9 and 11 Bushels Mean
          </h2>

          <p>
            Bagger capacity is quoted in bushels, and one US bushel is about 1.24 cubic feet. That makes a 6.5-bushel twin bagger about 8 cubic feet of space, a 9-bushel triple bagger about 11 cubic feet, and an 11-bushel triple bagger about 13.7 cubic feet. For comparison, a large tow-behind lawn sweeper such as the Agri-Fab 45-0492 in our <a href="/best-lawn-sweeper/">lawn sweeper guide</a> holds around 25 cubic feet, roughly double the biggest zero turn bagger here.
          </p>

