        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If bagging is a big part of your year, buy the mower whose factory bagger matches your yard. For a leaf-heavy acre or two, that means a 9- or 11-bushel triple bagger: Cub Cadet's 49A70001100 on a 48-inch Ultima ZTX, or Husqvarna's 591111401 on a fabricated Z254F. For a smaller lawn, a 6.5-bushel twin bagger on a Cub Cadet ZT1 or an EGO Z6 is enough.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Check the model number and deck type before you order, fit the counterweights, use high-lift blades, and bag when things are dry. If your fall means heavy wet leaves over several acres, no passive bagger will keep up, and a powered bagger or a tow-behind sweeper is the better tool.
